  "codebook": {
    "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator explicitly attributes a positive outcome, action, or achievement to their own efforts, advocacy, or legislative work.",
    "clarification": "Credit-claiming is identified when a senator uses language such as 'I secured,' 'I helped,' 'I authored,' 'I fought for,' or similar phrases that directly link their personal or legislative actions to a tangible result, funding, or policy change. It includes both direct claims of responsibility for outcomes and indirect claims where the senator highlights their role in achieving a specific goal.",
