        "explanation": "Senator Schumer explicitly claims credit for announcing federal grants for Westchester County fire departments, stating, 'I have Pushed for Additional Funding for Assistance to Fire Departments,' and linking his advocacy to the outcome."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator merely discusses, criticizes, or advocates for an issue without explicitly linking their actions to a specific outcome. It also does not include general statements of support, praise for others, or non-specific calls to action. Additionally, credit-claiming does not apply when the senator is simply reporting on an event or outcome without attributing it to their own efforts.",
